Z||000000||montage||05-19-2001||07:19 AM||||A while back I did a search on the forum for the stock offsets on a 1988 Formula. I found a few conflicting figures but the majority of the offsets were 45mm front and 35 mm rear. Yesterday I had some right front brake problems and pulled the wheel off (turns out the previous owner didn't seat the slider rubber seal properly and the slider is seized). I just happened to look in the inside of the wheel and cast there are the numbers 16X6 37mm. Is this the proper offset for the front of 88's? I hate to beat a dead horse but can anybody comment on the front and rear stock offsets for an 88? Thanks||||reg||1
